# Key Takeaways

- Use a **HashSet** when only membership matters.
- Build the lookup structure **once**, then perform constant-time queries.
- Avoid repeated linear searches over an unchanging collection.
- Remember that character comparisons are **case-sensitive**.
- This membership-checking pattern appears repeatedly in array, string, graph, and set-based interview problems.

